    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-τηκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>overlaid with gold,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανον χρυσοῦν, οὐ γὰρ ἐπίτηκτόν
					τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					96
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>with gold</i> or <i>gilded ornaments laid on,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρατὴρ ὑπάργυρος ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1386.16
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στλεγγίδιον ἐ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1544.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>counterfeit,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτηκτα φιλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.186
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>) ; <i>'veneer',</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				7.1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
